\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Latent geometry of the pilot under the provisional ontology (log-mel pooled embeddings; illustrative, not evidence). Left: pairwise distance matrix over four anchors (\texttt  {A1}--\texttt  {A4}) and their variants. Right: metric MDS of the same embeddings. Within-anchor variants form blocks and clusters, while cross-anchor distances are larger, and the two tempo settings span a wide range---consistent with the \texttt  {mixed} prior and with the need to estimate the tempo boundary from humans.}}{10}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pilot_geometry}{{3}{10}{Latent geometry of the pilot under the provisional ontology (log-mel pooled embeddings; illustrative, not evidence). Left: pairwise distance matrix over four anchors (\texttt {A1}--\texttt {A4}) and their variants. Right: metric MDS of the same embeddings. Within-anchor variants form blocks and clusters, while cross-anchor distances are larger, and the two tempo settings span a wide range---consistent with the \texttt {mixed} prior and with the need to estimate the tempo boundary from humans}{figure.3}{}}
